  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 60.0,
      "end": 84.94000244140625,
      "text": "PRABHUPĀDA Good luck, Tanu. How are you?"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.94000244140625,
      "end": 108.94000244140625,
      "text": "So today we will multiply numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.94000244140625,
      "end": 119.94000244140625,
      "text": "In grade five, we multiplied three-digit number by a two-digit number without regrouping."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.94000244140625,
      "end": 132.94000244140625,
      "text": "I will show you an example."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.94000244140625,
      "end": 144.94000244140625,
      "text": "When multiplying, how do we arrange the numbers? We arrange vertically."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.94000244140625,
      "end": 154.94000244140625,
      "text": "So we first multiply starting from the ones, then we go to the tens, then we go to the hundreds."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.94000244140625,
      "end": 169.94000244140625,
      "text": "So what is two times five? Ten. Zero, thirty-one. Five times seven? That's five plus one. That is three."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.94000244140625,
      "end": 181.94000244140625,
      "text": "Three, thirty-three. Five times three? Eighteen plus three? Eighteen. Right here, eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.94000244140625,
      "end": 191.94000244140625,
      "text": "Now, when multiplying the second digit, first write zero. You write zero first when multiplying the second digit."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.94000244140625,
      "end": 204.94000244140625,
      "text": "So what is two times two? Four. Two times seven? Thirteen. Four, thirty-one. Four, how are you? Four, thirty-one."
    },
    {
      "start": 204.94000244140625,
      "end": 230.94000244140625,
      "text": "Two times three? Six plus one? Seven. Then you add."
    },
    {
      "start": 231.94000244140625,
      "end": 257.94000244140625,
      "text": "So we will now continue multiplying numbers. We will multiply four-digit numbers by two-digit numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 257.94000244140625,
      "end": 267.94000244140625,
      "text": "How are you?"
    },
    {
      "start": 267.94000244140625,
      "end": 287.94000244140625,
      "text": "Now let us multiply a four-digit number by a two-digit number."
    },
    {
      "start": 287.94000244140625,
      "end": 305.94000244140625,
      "text": "So we will now, when multiplying, how do we arrange the numbers? We arrange the numbers vertically."
    },
    {
      "start": 305.94000244140625,
      "end": 319.94000244140625,
      "text": "So we begin by multiplying. So in the ones, what is zero multiplied by three? Zero."
    },
    {
      "start": 319.94000244140625,
      "end": 329.94000244140625,
      "text": "In the tens, what is six multiplied by three? Eighteen. So eight, thirty-one."
    },
    {
      "start": 329.94000244140625,
      "end": 354.94000244140625,
      "text": "In the hundreds column, what is five multiplied by three? Fifteen plus one? Fifteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 354.94000244140625,
      "end": 370.94000244140625,
      "text": "We now multiply the number by two. Before multiplying, what do we do in the ones? We write zero here."
    },
    {
      "start": 370.94000244140625,
      "end": 385.94000244140625,
      "text": "What is two times zero? Zero. Two times six? Twelve. Twelve, two, thirty-one. Two, thirty-one. Two times five? Ten. Ten plus one? Eleven."
    },
    {
      "start": 385.94000244140625,
      "end": 400.94000244140625,
      "text": "Write eleven here, then you add."
    },
    {
      "start": 400.94000244140625,
      "end": 425.94000244140625,
      "text": "Zero multiplied by three? Zero."
    },
    {
      "start": 425.94000244140625,
      "end": 432.94000244140625,
      "text": "Six multiplied by three? Eighteen. Eight, thirty-one."
    },
    {
      "start": 432.94000244140625,
      "end": 441.94000244140625,
      "text": "Five multiplied by three? Fifteen plus one? Fifteen. Six, thirty-one."
    },
    {
      "start": 441.94000244140625,
      "end": 446.94000244140625,
      "text": "One multiplied by three? Plus one? Four."
    },
    {
      "start": 447.94000244140625,
      "end": 471.94000244140625,
      "text": "Zero, ten, two, thirty-one, two, thirty-one. Ten, eleven, one, thirty-one. Two plus one?"
    },
    {
      "start": 471.94000244140625,
      "end": 495.94000244140625,
      "text": "Zero."
    },
    {
      "start": 495.94000244140625,
      "end": 500.94000244140625,
      "text": "And the perpetrator, who am I?"
    },
    {
      "start": 500.94000244140625,
      "end": 502.94000244140625,
      "text": "Look, look, look."
    },
    {
      "start": 530.9400024414062,
      "end": 533.9400024414062,
      "text": "My name is Michael."
    },
